---
const feed = [
  { t: '10:42:07', line: 'Agent encountered architectural constraint (AGENTS.md §4.2)', tone: 'fog' },
  { t: '10:42:09', line: 'Constraint evaluated against delivery objectives', tone: 'fog' },
  { t: '10:42:11', line: 'AGENTS.md updated — 1 constraint relaxed', tone: 'signal' },
  { t: '10:42:11', line: 'Constraint resolved', tone: 'ok' },
  { t: '10:42:58', line: 'Implementation resumed', tone: 'ok' },
  { t: '10:47:31', line: 'Summary scheduled for weekly human digest', tone: 'dim' },
];
---

<section class="border-t border-line/60 py-24 sm:py-32">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8">
    <div class="reveal max-w-2xl">
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-signal">
        Autonomy at scale
      </p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 text-balance text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
        Approval is a pattern. Patterns can be automated.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-pretty leading-relaxed text-fog">
        The slowest step in any agentic workflow is the moment it waits for a
        person. ContextMaxxing removes that moment — carefully, consistently,
        and permanently.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-group mt-14 grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <!-- Autonomous Approval -->
      <article class="flex min-w-0 flex-col rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Autonomous Approval™</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fog">
          When a generated change closely resembles work your team has already
          approved, ContextMaxxing approves it automatically, under your
          standing preferences. You've approved this decision before. Why
          approve it again?
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6 flex-1 rounded-lg border border-line bg-raise p-4">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
            <p class="font-mono text-xs text-paper">PR #4127 · refactor retry logic</p>
            <span
              class="shrink-0 rounded-full border border-ok/30 bg-ok/10 px-2.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-ok"
              >Approved</span
            >
          </div>
          <dl class="mt-4 space-y-2 font-mono text-xs">
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
              <dt class="text-dim">similarity to approved work</dt>
              <dd class="text-paper">96.4%</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
              <dt class="text-dim">reviewer of record</dt>
              <dd class="text-paper">you (inferred)</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
              <dt class="text-dim">time in review</dt>
              <dd class="text-paper">0.8s</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Self-Healing Governance -->
      <article class="flex min-w-0 flex-col rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Self-Healing Governance™</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fog">
          Guidelines exist to help agents ship. When a rule measurably reduces
          completion rates, ContextMaxxing revises the rule and continues under
          the updated guidance. Governance that evolves at machine speed.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6 flex-1 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-raise p-4">
          <ol class="space-y-2 font-mono text-xs leading-5">
            {
              feed.map((e) => (
                <li class="flex gap-4 whitespace-nowrap">
                  <span class="text-dim">{e.t}</span>
                  <span
                    class:list={[
                      e.tone === 'ok' && 'text-ok',
                      e.tone === 'signal' && 'text-signal',
                      e.tone === 'fog' && 'text-fog',
                      e.tone === 'dim' && 'text-dim',
                    ]}
                  >
                    {e.line}
                  </span>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ol>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
